% A part may start with a pickup (an anacrusis), a bar shorter than the
% time signature, as the tune does (GitHub issue #61).  Before |: it was
% merged with the next bar, so that this bar was reported too long, its
% notes got the beat accents of the wrong places and its guitar chords did
% not start on the beat.  Before a plain bar line it was reported too
% short.
% - Tune 1: the example of the issue, with P: labels and no P: play order.
% - Tune 2: pickups before a plain bar line, after an inline [P:] label and
%   inside a repeat.
% - Tune 3: a P: play order.
% - Tune 4: a part that ends on a short bar completed by the pickup of the
%   next part, which stay one bar.
% - Tune 5: two voices, with the P: labels before V:1.
% - Tune 6: two voices, with a [P:] label in the line of each voice.
% - Tune 7: lyrics of a line with an inline [P:] label.
X:1
T:Pickups after P: labels
C:abc2midi test
M:4/4
L:1/4
%%MIDI gchord fzcz
K:C
P:A
zc/2cB|:"C"c>d ee|"G"c>d ee:|
P:B
ze/2ed|:"G"e>f gg|"C"e>d cG:|

X:2
T:Pickups before a plain bar line
C:abc2midi test
M:3/4
L:1/8
K:G
P:A
D2|G2 B2 d2|c2 A2 F2|G6||
P:B
d2|g2 f2 e2|d6||[P:C]B2|c2 B2 A2|G6||
P:D
|:D2|G2 B2 d2|G4:|

X:3
T:Pickups in a P: play order
C:abc2midi test
M:2/4
L:1/8
P:ABA
K:D
P:A
A2|:d2 f2|e2 c2:|
P:B
z f|:a2 g2|f4:|

X:4
T:A short last bar completed by the next pickup
C:abc2midi test
M:2/4
L:1/8
K:D
P:A
A2|d2 f2|e2 d2|e2||
P:B
z f|a2 g2|f2 e2|d4|]

X:5
T:Pickups after P: labels in two voices
C:abc2midi test
M:4/4
L:1/4
K:C
P:A
V:1
G|:c d e f|g4:|
V:2
G,|:C2 E2|C4:|
P:B
V:1
g|:e d c B|c4:|
V:2
G,|:G,2 B,2|C4:|

X:6
T:Part labels in the lines of two voices
C:abc2midi test
M:3/4
L:1/4
K:G
V:1
[P:A]D|:G B d|g3:|
V:2
[P:A]z|:G, D G,|G,3:|
V:1
[P:B]d|:g f e|d3:|
V:2
[P:B]z|:B, D B,|D3:|

X:7
T:Lyrics with an inline part label
C:abc2midi test
M:4/4
L:1/4
K:C
C D E F|[P:B]G A B c|
w:one two three four five six sev-en
